  "verbalization": "Ebastine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of indirect pathways that involve vasomotor rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Ebastine is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis, which in turn is linked to two other drugs—Mizolastine and Ramatroban—both of which are indicated for Allergic Rhinitis. This indicates a potential mechanism where Ebastine may influence the onset or severity of allergic rhinitis through its effects on vasomotor symptoms. The shared indication of Allergic Rhinitis across these pathways suggests a possible overlap in the biological mechanisms underlying these conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of vasomotor rhinitis as a common intermediary step, potentially linking Ebastine to allergic rhinitis via its impact on inflammatory or neurogenic pathways. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Ebastine may contribute to the development of allergic rhinitis through its association with vasomotor rhinitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
